 until steaming hot in center.', 'Note: Alternately, potatoes can be reheated in a slow-cooker. Take potatoes out of refrigerator about 3 1/2 hours before you plan to serve them. Place in slow-cooker. Dot with margarine or butter. Cook on low heat for 3 hours, stirring once or twice. They can be held an additional 30 minutes or more.']\", \"Images\": \"[]\", \"AggregatedRating_na\": 5.0, \"ReviewCount\": 2.0, \"Calories\": 242.8, \"FatContent\": 9.8, \"SaturatedFatContent\": 5.6, \"CholesterolContent\": 28.1, \"SodiumContent\": 283.6, \"CarbohydrateContent\": 34.3, \"FiberContent\": 4.2, \"SugarContent\": 2.6, \"ProteinContent\": 5.7, \"source\": \"foodcom\", \"PrepTime\": \"PT30M\", \"CookTime\": \"PT40M\", \"TotalTime\": \"PT1H10M\", \"PrepTime_Minutes\": 30.0, \"CookTime_Minutes\": 40.0, \"TotalTime_Minutes\": 70.0, \"RecipeIngredientParts\": \"['potatoes', 'cream cheese', 'sour cream', 'salt', 'black pepper', 'butter']\", \"RecipeIngredientParts_old\": \"['potatoes', 'cream cheese', 'sour cream', 'salt', 'black pepper', 'butter']\", \"ingredients_canonical\": \"['potato', 'cream cheese', 'sour cream', 'salt', 'black pepper', 'butter']\", \"ingredients_canonical_auto\": \"['potato', 'cream cheese', 'sour cream', 'salt', 'black pepper', 'butter']\", \"ingredients_canonical_final\": \"['potato', 'cream cheese', 'sour cream', 'salt', 'black pepper', 'butter']\", \"ingredients_canonical_final_le_5_replace\": \"['potato', 'cream cheese', 'sour cream', 'salt', 'black pepper', 'butter']\", \"EnergyFromFat\": 88.2, \"EnergyFromSaturatedFat\": 50.4, \"EnergyFromCarbs\": 137.2, \"EnergyFromProtein\": 22.8, \"SaturatedFatPercentEnergy\": 20.75782537067545, \"FatPercentEnergy\": 36.32619439868204, \"WHO_SatFat_Compliant\": false, \"WHO_Fat_Compliant\": false, \"WHO_Sodium_Compliant\": true, \"WHO_Score\": 1, \"WHO_Healthy\": false, \"Energy_kJ\": 1015.8752, \"A_score\": 11, \"C_score\": 7, \"FSA_Score\": 4, \"FSA_Healthy\": false, \"popularity_score\": 10.0, \"ID\": \"468557_foodcom\", \"WHO_binary\": false, \"FSA_binary\": false, \"FSA_binned\": 2, \"popularity_log\": 2.3978952727983707, \"cluster\": \"0\", \"pca1\": -0.9690677108570048, \"pca2\": -0.19532388978903453, \"protein_kcal\": 22.8, \"fat_kcal\": 88.2, \"carb_kcal\": 137.2, \"protein_pct\": 9.186140209508462, \"fat_pct\": 35.535858178888, \"net_carb_pct\": 55.27800161160354, \"satiety_score_raw\": 12.698979643990036, \"satiety\": 17.091046802701076, \"nutrient_density_raw\": 2.987190608232639, \"nutrient_density\": 39.26250938286099}, {\"RecipeId\": 312740, \"Name\": \"Caramelized Mango Tart With Mexican Chocolate and Pepitas\", \"RecipeInstructions\": \"['Caramelize the mangoes. In a large (12-inch) non-stick skillet over medium-high heat, melt the butter. When it begins to brown, add the mangoes. Stir frequently for a couple of minutes until the fruit releases its juice. Sprinkle the sugar over the mango and continue stirring frequently until all the liquid has evaporated and the mango has begun to caramelize, about 4 minutes. Cool.', 'Make the chocolate-pepita filling. Turn on the oven to 400\\u00b0F and position the rack in the middle. Scoop the 2 chocolates into a food processor. Pulse until finely chopped, then add the pepitas and continue pulsing until they, too, are finely chopped. Scrape down the sides, then scrape in the almond butter. Process until the mixture is smooth, scraping down the sides as needed.', 'Bake the tart. Unroll the puff pastry. (If you are using the widely available Pepperidge Farms puff pastry, the sheet will be 10x10 inches; if yours isn\\u2019t, cut it to that size). Cut into 2 rectangles 5 x 10 inches each and place them onto a baking sheet lined with parchment paper or a silicone mat. Spread the chocolate mixture over the puff pastry, leaving a full 1-inch border all around. Top with the cool mango slices in an even layer.  Bake until the pastry is richly brown and mango richly caramelized, about 25 minutes.']\", \"Images\": \"[]\", \"Aggre