ter with the bay leaf until they are soft but not mushy, probably 30-40 minutes.  You can add more water if they are drying out but need more time to cook.  When they are done, drain if there is any leftover water.', 'Add salt to flavor the lentils when they are done and remove the bay leaf.  Set aside. (You can probably do the rice and lentils mostly at the same time).', 'Slice the onions very thin.', 'Caramelize the onions in the 2 tbs olive oil, on a very low flame, until they are soft and golden, not brown and crisp.', 'Add the cumin, cinnamon, salt and pepper to the onions.', 'Now combine: fluff the rice with a fork.  Add the lentils and stir.  Stir in some of the onions and perhaps leave some to go on the top.']\", \"Images\": \"[]\", \"AggregatedRating_na\": 5.0, \"ReviewCount\": 2.0, \"Calories\": 264.9, \"FatContent\": 7.2, \"SaturatedFatContent\": 1.0, \"CholesterolContent\": 0.0, \"SodiumContent\": 445.8, \"CarbohydrateContent\": 42.1, \"FiberContent\": 7.0, \"SugarContent\": 1.6, \"ProteinContent\": 7.4, \"source\": \"foodcom\", \"PrepTime\": \"PT20M\", \"CookTime\": \"PT50M\", \"TotalTime\": \"PT1H10M\", \"PrepTime_Minutes\": 20.0, \"CookTime_Minutes\": 50.0, \"TotalTime_Minutes\": 70.0, \"RecipeIngredientParts\": \"['white rice', 'olive oil', 'water', 'garlic cloves', 'salt', 'brown lentils', 'bay leaf', 'water', 'olive oil', 'onions', 'cumin', 'ground cinnamon', 'salt']\", \"RecipeIngredientParts_old\": \"['white rice', 'olive oil', 'water', 'garlic cloves', 'salt', 'brown lentils', 'bay leaf', 'water', 'olive oil', 'onions', 'cumin', 'ground cinnamon', 'salt']\", \"ingredients_canonical\": \"['white rice', 'olive oil', 'water', 'garlic', 'salt', 'lentil', 'bay leaf', 'onion', 'cumin', 'cinnamon']\", \"ingredients_canonical_auto\": \"['white rice', 'olive oil', 'water', 'garlic', 'salt', 'lentil', 'bay leaf', 'onion', 'cumin', 'cinnamon']\", \"ingredients_canonical_final\": \"['white rice', 'olive oil', 'water', 'garlic', 'salt', 'lentil', 'bay leaf',