656041512231, \"satiety_score_raw\": 7.316939694849257, \"satiety\": 14.49515349954609, \"nutrient_density_raw\": 4.252769854530527, \"nutrient_density\": 40.552703119310614}, {\"RecipeId\": 504361, \"Name\": \"Norwegian Boller\", \"RecipeInstructions\": \"['Mix the warm milk (about 100F), melted butter, sugar and yeast together in a large bowl.  Let it stand for 10 mins unntil the yeast is foamy.  Add the salt and cardemon. Add the flour 1 cup at a time, stirring to mix after each addition.  Stir in the raisins if you are using them.  The dough will be pretty sticky at this point.', 'Cover and let the dough rise in a warm place for about an hour, or until doubled in size.', 'Punch down the dough and turn it out onto a floured surface. Sprinkle top with flour and knead briefly (for just a couple of minutes) Make sure you flour hands a lot to be able to do the next step. Break off pieces of dough about the size of a large golf ball and roll in your hands to make them round and smooth.', 'Place the balls of dough onto a greased cookie sheet and cover.  Let them rise for about 30-40 minutes.', 'Brush the tops with beaten egg white and bake in a preheated 350 F oven for 20 minutes, or until they are golden brown.  Cool about 15 minutes before eating and then enjoy with butter, or chese and meat, or just plain!']\", \"Images\": \"[]\", \"AggregatedRating_na\": 0.0, \"ReviewCount\": 1.0, \"Calories\": 382.4, \"FatContent\": 10.3, \"SaturatedFatContent\": 6.1, \"CholesterolContent\": 27.4, \"SodiumContent\": 293.2, \"CarbohydrateContent\": 63.8, \"FiberContent\": 2.2, \"SugarContent\": 16.8, \"ProteinContent\": 8.8, \"source\": \"foodcom\", \"PrepTime\": \"PT2H\", \"CookTime\": \"PT20M\", \"TotalTime\": \"PT2H20M\", \"PrepTime_Minutes\": 120.0, \"CookTime_Minutes\": 20.0, \"TotalTime_Minutes\": 140.0, \"RecipeIngredientParts\": \"['milk', 'butter', 'granulated sugar', 'active dry yeast', 'salt', 'cardamom', 'all-purpose flour', 'raisins']\", \"RecipeIngredientParts_old\": 