Split flounder in in half along centerline, coat with panko (season with salt and pepper if you wish) and saute in 2 tbsp butter and a little olive oil until just lightly brown - set aside.', \\\"2. For the sauce:  Make a bechamel by melting the remaining butter and adding the flour --  cook for a minute or two and then gently add the milk.  You can warm the milk before adding, but we usually don't.  Stir until thickened and set aside.\\\", '3.  Separately saute the green onions and mushrooms until soft in a bit more of the butter --  can substitute olive oil for the butter if you wish.', '4.  Add  these to the bechamel sauce and combine with the marsala.', \\\"5.  Place a bit of the sauce in the bottom of the shell or gratin dish.  Gently fold the flounder in half and place on top of the sauce.  Add some more sauce on top and sprinkle with the regular breadcrumbs and a dusting of parmesan.  You can add a tiny bit of butter on the top to assist in browning, but we really don't think it's necessary.\\\", '6.  Place under broiler until warm and lightly browned. Serve immediately - though, as mentioned you can hold them for 24 hours or freeze prior to the broiling process.']\", \"Images\": \"[]\", \"AggregatedRating_na\": 0.0, \"ReviewCount\": 0.0, \"Calories\": 179.8, \"FatContent\": 11.7, \"SaturatedFatContent\": 5.3, \"CholesterolContent\": 20.9, \"SodiumContent\": 178.7, \"CarbohydrateContent\": 13.2, \"FiberContent\": 0.8, \"SugarContent\": 3.5, \"ProteinContent\": 4.1, \"source\": \"foodcom\", \"PrepTime\": \"PT45M\", \"CookTime\": \"PT8M\", \"TotalTime\": \"PT53M\", \"PrepTime_Minutes\": 45.0, \"CookTime_Minutes\": 8.0, \"TotalTime_Minutes\": 53.0, \"RecipeIngredientParts\": \"['panko breadcrumbs', 'parmesan cheese', 'butter', 'olive oil', 'flour', 'green onions', 'cremini mushrooms', 'marsala']\", \"RecipeIngredientParts_old\": \"['panko breadcrumbs', 'parmesan cheese', 'butter', 'olive oil', 'flour', 'green onions', 'cremini mushrooms', 'marsala']\", \"ingredi