apeno Spread\", \"RecipeInstructions\": \"['Preheat oven to 350F degrees.', 'Using a metal pie plate, place the pine nuts, chili powder, and cumin in the center of the plate.', 'Bake in preheated oven for about 6 minutes or until spices are fragrant and begin to darken (careful not to burn!); let cool completely.', 'Place the green onion, garlic, and cilantro in a food processor and whir until chopped.', 'Add the jalapeno and the nut/spice mixture and whir until nuts are chopped.', 'Add the cream cheese, goat cheese, sour cream or yogurt, and lime juice and whir until blended.', 'Place in covered container and refrigerate for at least 8 hours, but the longer you can leave it before serving the better- 24 hours is preferred.', 'Scrape spread into a serving bowl and serve with raw veggies (celery, cauliflower, broccoli, endive, carrot, etc).', 'Makes about 1 cup.']\", \"Images\": \"[]\", \"AggregatedRating_na\": 0.0, \"ReviewCount\": 0.0, \"Calories\": 988.2, \"FatContent\": 92.5, \"SaturatedFatContent\": 45.9, \"CholesterolContent\": 194.8, \"SodiumContent\": 1058.7, \"CarbohydrateContent\": 18.7, \"FiberContent\": 3.4, \"SugarContent\": 4.3, \"ProteinContent\": 28.7, \"source\": \"foodcom\", \"PrepTime\": \"PT24H\", \"CookTime\": \"PT6M\", \"TotalTime\": \"PT24H6M\", \"PrepTime_Minutes\": 1440.0, \"CookTime_Minutes\": 6.0, \"TotalTime_Minutes\": 1446.0, \"RecipeIngredientParts\": \"['pine nuts', 'chili powder', 'ground cumin', 'green onion', 'garlic', 'fresh cilantro', 'cream cheese', 'sour cream', 'plain yogurt', 'lime juice']\", \"RecipeIngredientParts_old\": \"['pine nuts', 'chili powder', 'ground cumin', 'green onion', 'garlic', 'fresh cilantro', 'cream cheese', 'sour cream', 'plain yogurt', 'lime juice']\", \"ingredients_canonical\": \"['pine nut', 'chili powder', 'cumin', 'green onion', 'garlic', 'cilantro', 'cream cheese', 'sour cream', 'yogurt', 'lime juice']\", \"ingredients_canonical_auto\": \"['pine nut', 'chili powder', 'cumin', 'green onion', 'garlic', 