r several minutes, stirring constantly.', 'Season with marjoram, tarragon, and basil, salt and pepper. Cook, stirring occasionally, until the cabbage is wilted and the onions are soft. Remove from the pan and set aside.', 'Add another tablespoon of butter to the pan and saute the mushrooms lightly for about 5 to 6 minutes, stirring constantly.', 'Spread the softened cream cheese in the bottom of the pie shell. 9. Arrange the egg slices in a layer over the cheese. Sprinkle them with chopped dill, then cover them with the cabbage.', 'Make a final layer of the sauteed mushrooms and cover with the circle of pastry. Seal and flute the edges of the crust.', 'With a sharp knife, cut a few short slashes through the top crust.', 'Bake in the preheated oven for 12 minutes. Reduce temperature to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C) and bake for 20 to 25 minutes, or until golden brown.']\", \"Images\": \"[]\", \"AggregatedRating_na\": 0.0, \"ReviewCount\": 0.0, \"Calories\": 295.9, \"FatContent\": 18.7, \"SaturatedFatContent\": 10.8, \"CholesterolContent\": 152.4, \"SodiumContent\": 465.0, \"CarbohydrateContent\": 23.9, \"FiberContent\": 3.1, \"SugarContent\": 5.2, \"ProteinContent\": 9.7, \"source\": \"foodcom\", \"PrepTime\": \"PT50M\", \"CookTime\": \"PT40M\", \"TotalTime\": \"PT1H30M\", \"PrepTime_Minutes\": 50.0, \"CookTime_Minutes\": 40.0, \"TotalTime_Minutes\": 90.0, \"RecipeIngredientParts\": \"['hard-boiled eggs', 'all-purpose flour', 'white sugar', 'salt', 'butter', 'cream cheese', 'onion', 'head of cabbage', 'dried marjoram', 'dried tarragon', 'dried basil leaves', 'butter', 'fresh mushrooms', 'dried dill weed']\", \"RecipeIngredientParts_old\": \"['hard-boiled eggs', 'all-purpose flour', 'white sugar', 'salt', 'butter', 'cream cheese', 'onion', 'head of cabbage', 'dried marjoram', 'dried tarragon', 'dried basil leaves', 'butter', 'fresh mushrooms', 'dried dill weed']\", \"ingredients_canonical\": \"['egg', 'all purpose flour', 'sugar', 'salt', 'butter', 'cream cheese', 'on