ntil the batter is smooth. The batter consistency should be quite thick, so add the beer accordingly.', 'Season the fish with the coriander, chipotle powder and salt.', \\\"Working in batches, drop some of the seasoned fish into the bowl with the batter and coat completely. Using a fork or tongs, gently remove the fish from the batter and carefully place into the hot oil. Cook fish for 4-5 minutes, turning continuously, until golden and crispy all over. Cook them in batches if you need to;  you don't want to overcrowd the pot. Remove pieces to a paper towel-lined platter.\\\", 'While the fish is frying, prepare the cabbage mixture: place a large skillet over high heat with two turns of the pan of vegetable oil, about two tablespoons. Once hot, add the shredded cabbage and sliced onions, and cook for 2-3 minutes, stirring frequently. Season with some salt, pepper and juice of one lime.', 'Add 2-3 pieces of the fish to a tortilla, then top with the avocado sauce and cabbage salad. Fold it and eat it up!']\", \"Images\": \"[]\", \"AggregatedRating_na\": 0.0, \"ReviewCount\": 0.0, \"Calories\": 857.3, \"FatContent\": 36.5, \"SaturatedFatContent\": 7.3, \"CholesterolContent\": 79.4, \"SodiumContent\": 1429.8, \"CarbohydrateContent\": 88.4, \"FiberContent\": 12.8, \"SugarContent\": 5.7, \"ProteinContent\": 45.2, \"source\": \"foodcom\", \"PrepTime\": \"PT30M\", \"CookTime\": \"PT10M\", \"TotalTime\": \"PT40M\", \"PrepTime_Minutes\": 30.0, \"CookTime_Minutes\": 10.0, \"TotalTime_Minutes\": 40.0, \"RecipeIngredientParts\": \"['flour tortillas', 'avocados', 'garlic clove', 'sour cream', 'limes, juice of', 'flour', 'salt', 'sugar', 'baking powder', 'beer', 'sesame seeds', 'ground coriander', 'salt', 'napa cabbage', 'red onion']\", \"RecipeIngredientParts_old\": \"['flour tortillas', 'avocados', 'garlic clove', 'sour cream', 'limes, juice of', 'flour', 'salt', 'sugar', 'baking powder', 'beer', 'sesame seeds', 'ground coriander', 'salt', 'napa cabbage', 'red onion']\", \"ingred