ce them in the oven and bake for 20 minutes.', 'Meanwhile, prepare the gravy. Melt the butter in a saucepan on medium heat. Add the shallot and garlic. Let them cook for 2 minutes until translucent, but not brown. Add the flour and quickly stir with a spoon. Add a little broth if gets too clumpy.', 'Let the mixture cook until it turns light brown. Add the vegetable broth, soy sauce, and cayenne pepper. Bring the gravy to a boil, then turn down the heat and let it cook for about 5 minutes, stirring occasionally. Taste it, adding salt and pepper as needed. Turn down the heat to very low, just enough to keep the gravy warm until the fries come out of the oven.', 'Dice the cheese.', 'After the fries have baked for 20 minutes, remove them from the oven. Lift them with a spatula and test their tenderness with a fork. If it goes through easily, the fries are ready. If you want them a little more crispy, flip them over and put them back in the over for a few more minutes.', 'Once they\\u2019re done, pile one layer of fries onto a plate. Top with cheese and then the hot gravy. Repeat with a second layer before sprinkling with scallions and more freshly ground black pepper.']\", \"Images\": \"['https://img.sndimg.com/food/image/upload/w_555,h_416,c_fit,fl_progressive,q_95/v1/img/recipes/51/78/46/BKN9rVETnqVjW3zddIJ1_0S9A4664.jpg', 'https://img.sndimg.com/food/image/upload/w_555,h_416,c_fit,fl_progressive,q_95/v1/img/recipes/51/78/46/sN6AgmITH20iMh0zViUJ_0279922_GK_Montreal-Style-Poutine-4x3_v2_H.jpg', 'https://img.sndimg.com/food/image/upload/w_555,h_416,c_fit,fl_progressive,q_95/v1/img/recipes/51/78/46/VaALnIHGSISL3ykenXK2_0S9A4707.jpg', 'https://img.sndimg.com/food/image/upload/w_555,h_416,c_fit,fl_progressive,q_95/v1/img/recipes/51/78/46/30cgacMwQ1eES31p4pjq_0S9A4690.jpg']\", \"AggregatedRating_na\": 5.0, \"ReviewCount\": 4.0, \"Calories\": 517.3, \"FatContent\": 25.6, \"SaturatedFatContent\": 9.2, \"CholesterolContent\": 30.5, \"SodiumContent\": 292.8, \"CarbohydrateConte