y\": 29.123546700260132, \"nutrient_density_raw\": 43.58443473302604, \"nutrient_density\": 80.64933698780425}, {\"RecipeId\": 173463, \"Name\": \"Hamam Mahshi Bi Burghul-Cornish Game Hens W/Bulgur &amp; Raisins\", \"RecipeInstructions\": \"['To prepare the hens, sprinkle with 1/2 teaspoon salt and 1/4 teaspoon pepper. Place the onion and next 5 ingredients (onion through allspice) in a food processor; process until smooth. Combine hens and onion mixture in a large zip-top plastic bag. Seal bag; marinate in refrigerator 1 hour, turning bag occasionally. Remove the hens from the bag; discard marinade.', 'Preheat oven to 400\\u00b0F.', 'Place hens on a broiler pan coated with cooking spray; bake at 400\\u00b0F for 35 minutes or until thermometer registers 180\\u00b0F.', 'To prepare the bulgur, soak currants in a bowl of water 15 minutes. Drain; set aside. Bring broth to a boil in a medium saucepan. Add the bulgur, 1 1/2 teaspoons cinnamon,1/2 teaspoon salt, and 1/4 teaspoon pepper; cover, reduce heat, and simmer 15 minutes or until liquid is absorbed. Stir in currants, pine nuts, and butter.', 'Yield: 6 servings (serving size: 1/2 Cornish hen and 1 1/2 cups bulgur mixture).']\", \"Images\": \"[]\", \"AggregatedRating_na\": 5.0, \"ReviewCount\": 1.0, \"Calories\": 776.8, \"FatContent\": 27.6, \"SaturatedFatContent\": 7.6, \"CholesterolContent\": 325.1, \"SodiumContent\": 671.9, \"CarbohydrateContent\": 57.3, \"FiberContent\": 11.7, \"SugarContent\": 15.1, \"ProteinContent\": 76.4, \"source\": \"foodcom\", \"PrepTime\": \"PT30M\", \"CookTime\": \"PT1H\", \"TotalTime\": \"PT1H30M\", \"PrepTime_Minutes\": 30.0, \"CookTime_Minutes\": 60.0, \"TotalTime_Minutes\": 90.0, \"RecipeIngredientParts\": \"['salt', 'black pepper', 'onions', 'fresh lemon juice', 'ground cardamom', 'ground cinnamon', 'ground allspice', 'currants', 'bulgur', 'ground cinnamon', 'salt', 'black pepper', 'pine nuts', 'butter']\", \"RecipeIngredientParts_old\": \"['salt', 'black pepper', 'onions', 'fresh lemon juice', 'ground cardamom', 'ground cinnamon', 'ground allspice', 'currants', 'bulgur', 'ground cinnamon', 'salt', 'black pepper', 'pine nuts', 'butter']\", \"ingredients_canonical\": \"['salt', 'black pepper', 'onion', 'lemon juice', 'cardamom', 'cinnamon', 'allspice', 'currant', 'bulgur', 'pine nut', 'butter']\", \"ingredients_canonical_auto\": \"['salt', 'black pepper', 'onion', 'lemon juice', 'cardamom', 'cinnamon', 'allspice', 'currant', 'bulgur', 'pine nut', 'butter']\", \"ingredients_canonical_final\": \"['salt', 'black pepper', 'onion', 'lemon juice', 'cardamom', 'cinnamon', 'allspice', 'currant', 'bulgur', 'pine nut', 'butter']\", \"ingredients_canonical_final_le_5_replace\": \"['salt', 'black pepper', 'onion', 'lemon juice', 'cardamom', 'cinnamon', 'allspice', 'currant', 'bulgur', 'pine nut', 'butter']\", \"EnergyFromFat\": 248.4, \"EnergyFromSaturatedFat\": 68.39999999999999, \"EnergyFromCarbs\": 229.2, \"EnergyFromProtein\": 305.6, \"SaturatedFatPercentEnergy\": 8.805355303810504, \"FatPercentEnergy\": 31.9773429454171, \"WHO_SatFat_Compliant\": true, \"WHO_Fat_Compliant\": false, \"WHO_Sodium_Compliant\": false, \"WHO_Score\": 1, \"WHO_Healthy\": false, \"Energy_kJ\": 3250.1312, \"A_score\": 26, \"C_score\": 10, \"FSA_Score\": 16, \"FSA_Healthy\": false, \"popularity_score\": 5.0, \"ID\": \"173463_foodcom\", \"WHO_binary\": false, \"FSA_binary\": false, \"FSA_binned\": 0, \"popularity_log\": 1.791759469228055, \"cluster\": \"3\", \"pca1\": 3.025027504913393, \"pca2\": -1.7818163722920386, \"protein_kcal\": 305.6, \"fat_kcal\": 248.4, \"carb_kcal\": 229.2, \"protein_pct\": 39.019407558733405, \"fat_pct\": 31.716036772216544, \"net_carb_pct\": 29.264555669050047, \"satiety_score_raw\": 44.70228139689996, \"satiety\": 32.52704458129246, \"nutrient_density_raw\": 41.62652966146531, \"nutrient_density\": 78.65335225015944}, {\"RecipeId\": 333774, \"Name\": \"Char-Crusted Rib Eye, Garlic Butter Mushrooms &amp; Yukon Gold\", \"RecipeInstructions\": \"['Remove steak from refrigerator 45 minutes prior to grilling.  Apply Char Crust Roasted Garlic and Peppercorn rub and let sit to warm to room temperature.  Heat grill to accomplish searing.  Put steak on grill and turn 90\\u00b0 one minute later.  After another minute flip the steak over and after another minute turn steak 90\\u00b0 again to accomplish the great grill marks.  Turn grill down to 350\\u00b0 and continue to grill for another 10-15 minutes depending on your desired degree of doneness, flipping steak half way through.  Baste steak with a little EV olive oil when you turn the heat down and when you flip it to help maintain the beautiful char and moistness.  When steak is done to your taste, remove from grill and let sit for 3-4 minutes covered with aluminum foil.', 'A steak of this quality should be enjoyed with a great Cabernet Sauvignon.', 'Sides:', 'Garlic-butter Mushrooms.', 'Garlic-butter marinade: (Mix up in a small ramekin).', '1 ounce of EV olive oil.', '1 tsp butter.', '1 clove garlic finely chopped.', '1/8 tsp fresh cracked pepper.', '1/8 tsp salt.', 'Remove the stems from 4-6 mushrooms and dredge the mushroom caps well in the garlic butter mixture.  Place them head down on a 12\\\\\\\\', ' square of aluminum foil and wrap up and seal into a packet for the grill.  Put this packet on the grill when your turn the heat down to 350\\u00b0 after searing your steak and they should be done perfectly in about 12-15 minutes.', 'Seasoned Yukon Gold.', 'After a good scrubbing, stab the Yukon Gold with a fork several times. Rub the skin with a small amount of EV olive oil to moisten it, then season the skin with salt, pepper and some chive flakes and wrap the potato in aluminum foil.  The potato will take about an hour on the grill @ 350\\u00b0 so make your cooking plans accordingly.', 'Bon Appetite!']\", \"Images\": \"[]\", \"AggregatedRating_na\": 5.0, \"ReviewCount\": 1.0, \"Calories\": 1317.8, \"FatContent\": 78.5, \"SaturatedFatContent\": 31.6, \"Cholestero